scope: |
  MEASURED FIRST, in a throwaway lab with a fake origin and a `pre-push` hook that refuses (standing
  in for the overlap guard rejecting a stranger's parked claim): `scripts/coord-release` exits 1 and
  LEAVES ITS COMMIT ON SHARED MAIN — 1 parked, claim file gone locally, ledger row gone, while both
  still exist on origin. `scripts/coord-claim` learned to roll back on 2026-08-07; this script never
  did. A parked coordination commit is refused FOR A STRANGER, because the shared checkout pushes all
  of local main and the guard validates every claim in remote_tip..local_tip — BUGS
  shared-main-is-one-working-tree-for-every-agent recorded three such landmines in one day.

  Second defect in the same three lines: the refusal asserts "main moved. Re-run after: git fetch &&
  git merge --ff-only" without looking. The refusal that actually happens here is the OTHER one, and
  fetching does nothing for it — the advice sends the reader in a circle while everyone is blocked.

  NARROW: the push branch of one script, plus cases 6 and 7 in the lab that already exists for it.
  Widened to scripts/SPRINT.md + scripts/BUGS.md for the board row and for the remaining kind of
  landmine, which is hand-made claim-updates and has no tool at all.

  WIDENED AGAIN to scripts/smoke-ci.ssc, before the edit. The gate I extended IS NOT RUN BY
  ANYTHING: `tests/coord/coord-release-refuses-unpushed-work.sh` appears in no runner, so cases 6
  and 7 would have guarded nothing. Census of its directory: SIX of eleven tests/coord/*.sh are
  invoked by nothing — also claim-activity-overrides-heartbeat, coord-claim-runs,
  coord-release-evidence-level, coord-status-ledger-marker, heartbeat-threshold-single-source. All
  six PASS today and cost 9.9 s together (57ms/1835/2953/4316/547/171), i.e. 1.3% of a 750 s suite,
  so wiring them cannot surprise anybody with a red. An instance of BUGS orphaned-e2e-gates-52,
  measured rather than asserted.
